        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0456" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg386"/>

                <head>No. 203.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sargent to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15, 1883</date>.
                        (Received July 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 102½, of
                    the 31st March last, concerning the adjustment of the Venezuela debts, I have
                    now the honor to inclose a copy of a note in accordance with the same, addressed
                    by me to Count Hatzfeldt on the 30th April, and also a copy, with translation,
                    of his excellency’s reply of the 14th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. A. SARGENT.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d203-a1.xml" xpointer="d203-a1"/>
